  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Peter Thornton is an American lighting entrepreneur who founded Focal Point, the Chicago architectural lighting manufacturer developed with his children. He previously co-founded Fail-Safe with Edward Claffy and sold that business to Cooper Industries. Focal Point grew as a family-owned manufacturer before joining Legrand, supplying lighting for workplaces and other commercial buildings.",
