    "word_count": 52,
    "html": "<p>Peter Thornton is an American lighting entrepreneur who founded Focal Point, the Chicago architectural lighting manufacturer developed with his children. He previously co-founded Fail-Safe with Edward Claffy and sold that business to Cooper Industries. Focal Point grew as a family-owned manufacturer before joining Legrand, supplying lighting for workplaces and other commercial buildings.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Peter Thornton’s support for youth sailing draws on his childhood in Chicago’s South Shore neighbourhood. As a boy, he fished with his mother beside Jackson Park and dreamed of getting out on the water. He later became a competitive sailor, winning the Race to Mackinac’s first-to-finish trophy on several occasions.\n\nWith his wife, Marijane, Thornton supports sailing education through the CYC Foundation and its partnership with Jackson Park’s Open Horizons programme. The couple provided four cruises for sailing-school campers in one summer. One camper used the visit to ask the captain about obtaining a professional licence.",
    "confidence": {
      "score": 78,
      "band": "medium",
      "reason": "Primary donor account, programme report and official trophy results support childhood, racing and joint youth access; identity limitation retained."
    },
    "source_ids": [
