      "S8"
    ],
    "word_count": 96,
    "html": "<p>Peter Thornton’s support for youth sailing draws on his childhood in Chicago’s South Shore neighbourhood. As a boy, he fished with his mother beside Jackson Park and dreamed of getting out on the water. He later became a competitive sailor, winning the Race to Mackinac’s first-to-finish trophy on several occasions.</p>\r\n<p>With his wife, Marijane, Thornton supports sailing education through the CYC Foundation and its partnership with Jackson Park’s Open Horizons programme. The couple provided four cruises for sailing-school campers in one summer. One camper used the visit to ask the captain about obtaining a professional licence.</p>\r\n"
  },
